{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261107T014701Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "c6753801124926054dd45c4c", "title": "Accelerating Reinforcement Learning Weight Refit with the Reshard Collective", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/accelerating-reinforcement-learning-weight-refit-with-the-reshard-collective/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-11-06T18:03:26+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.9475, "worthiness_confidence": 0.82, "final_score": 0.9475, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 12986, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA introduced Reshard, a new collective communication operation optimizing weight synchronization between training and inference GPUs during RL post-training. Current gather-and-broadcast approaches create redundant communication payloads reaching ~10TB per refit for trillion-parameter models like Qwen and DeepSeek v3. Reshard reformulates weight refit as a DTensor-to-DTensor transfer problem, eliminating redundancy by transferring each weight shard exactly once across the network while leveraging NVLink for local replication. The open-source NCCL M2N Reshard implementation achieves 2.7x to 5.7x speedup over conventional methods, completing trillion-parameter refits in 4.3 seconds. Key takeaway: use Reshard for dominant feed-forward weights in NeMo RL by setting `refit_transport: nccl_reshard`.", "jev_ms": 158.8, "jev_input_tokens": 3376, "jev_cost": 0.000141792, "llm_ms": 2466.7, "llm_cost": 0.004232, "errors": []}
