{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261107T014701Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "e572010b9c959715946853a3", "title": "Zero Mismatch, Simple Async RL: REINFORCE Zero, DeepSeek-V4.1 and Kimi K3.1", "url": "https://vllm.ai/blog/2026-11-06-zero-mismatch-async-rl", "source": "vLLM Blog", "published": "2026-11-06T00:00:00+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 1.0, "worthiness_confidence": 1.0, "final_score": 1.0, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 12155, "delivered": true, "summary": "REINFORCE Zero introduces kernel alignment to enable stable asynchronous RL at high policy lag. The approach decomposes the rollout-to-learner gap into weight lag (corrected by unclipped importance sampling) and kernel mismatch (eliminated by aligning rollout and training kernels). On DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash and Kimi K3.1, REINFORCE Zero achieves 2.40× synchronous training throughput while learning at lag 64, maintaining flat KL divergence through 20,000 updates. The key insight: remove kernel mismatch first, then plain unclipped IS stabilizes training without rejection gates or clipping.", "jev_ms": 117.7, "jev_input_tokens": 4022, "jev_cost": 0.000168924, "llm_ms": 5701.9, "llm_cost": 0.004661, "errors": []}
